---
description: |
  Turns Sigma detection findings into stage records for `socprime::correlate`.

  A finding becomes a record for the first stage whose Sigma rule IDs contain
  `finding_info.analytic.uid`, keyed by the lowercase hostname of its source
  event. Findings of other rules and findings without a hostname are dropped.
  Each record carries `time`, `stage`, `entity`, the source event in `event`,
  and a summary of the Detection Finding in `finding`.
args:
  named:
    - name: stages
      description: |
        A record from stage name to the list of Sigma rule IDs that cover the
        stage, such as `socprime::$hos.kimsuky_diplomats.stages`.
---

_stage = $stages.entries().where(stage => finding_info.analytic.uid in stage.value)[0].key
where _stage != null
this = {
  time: evidences[0].data.time? else time,
  stage: _stage,
  entity: {host: evidences[0].data.device?.hostname?.to_lower()},
  event: evidences[0].data,
  finding: {
    uid: finding_info.uid,
    type_uid: type_uid,
    title: finding_info.title,
    analytic: finding_info.analytic,
    severity_id: severity_id,
    attacks: finding_info.attacks?,
    observables: observables?,
  },
}
where entity.host != null
